      "content": "10.1 Number System"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Binary Number System operates on Base 2 using only digits 0 and 1.",
        "Octal Number System operates on Base 8 using digits 0 through 7.",
        "Decimal Number System operates on Base 10 using standard digits 0 through 9.",
        "Hexadecimal Number System operates on Base 16 using digits 0-9 and letters A-F.",
        "ASCII stands for American Standard Code for Information Interchange used for character encoding."
